title: '[pallet-revive] PolkaVM 0.38: the interpreter meters compilation, new ref time per gas'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    PolkaVM is bumped from 0.36 to 0.38 (`polkavm`, `polkavm-common`, `polkavm-derive`,
    `polkavm-linker`). PolkaVM 0.38 lets the interpreter charge gas for compiling contract code,
    and `pallet-revive` configures that cost from its benchmarks. The `pallet-revive`
    fixtures build template follows the workspace pin.

    Compilation cost, charged as PolkaVM gas by the interpreter:

    - Per compiled basic block of `n` instructions:
      `per_block + ceil(n * per_instruction_millis / 1000)`. Every block a contract enters is
      charged when it is compiled, and again whenever it is compiled after the interpreter
      dropped its compiled code.
    - Per byte of the code section: `ceil(code_len * per_code_byte_millis / 1000)`, charged when
      the interpreter allocates or rewrites its map of compiled blocks. The first allocation of a
      call is paid by the caller with the code load, and the callee's instance starts with a gas
      credit of the same size, which that allocation consumes. The contract pays the allocation
      again on its first compilation after a sub-call during which a PVM frame started, and the
      rewrites after many cache resets.
    - When a PVM frame starts, the innermost PVM frame that waits on a sub-call drops its
      compiled code and its map of compiled blocks. A PVM frame starts for a call, delegate call
      or instantiation of a PVM contract, also when a pre-compile or an EVM contract makes it.
      Pre-compile calls that start no PVM frame, transfers to accounts without code and calls to
      EVM contracts that start no PVM frame keep the caller's compiled code.
    - The values come from the slopes of `interpreter_compile_per_instruction`,
      `interpreter_compile_per_block` and `interpreter_code_map_per_byte`, converted with the ref
      time per gas and rounded up. `per_block` is the `interpreter_compile_per_block` slope
      minus the `interpreter_compile_per_instruction` slope and one gas.
    - The pallet's `integrity_test` asserts that `per_block`, `per_instruction_millis` and
      `per_code_byte_millis` are larger than 0. So the `interpreter_compile_per_block` slope must
      exceed the `interpreter_compile_per_instruction` slope plus one gas, and the
      `interpreter_compile_per_instruction` and `interpreter_code_map_per_byte` slopes must not
      be 0.
    - Loading PVM code for a call is charged to the caller (the calling frame, or the transaction
      for the first frame) at the slope of `call_with_pvm_code_per_byte` per byte of the code
      blob. The benchmark includes the callee's first allocation of the map of compiled blocks,
      so the pallet's `integrity_test` asserts that its ref time slope is at least the
      `interpreter_code_map_per_byte` slope.
    - Compiling a block and allocating or rewriting the map of compiled blocks can leave the
      interpreter's gas negative. `pallet-revive` then charges all the ref time it handed to the
      interpreter and fails the call frame with `OutOfGas`. The proof size is not affected.

    Ref time per PolkaVM gas, the largest of nine measurements:

    - `instr_load_chain_0` to `instr_load_chain_7` (dependent loads, one variant per offset of
      the loaded value within a 64 byte cache line) and `instr_indirect_jump` (indirect jumps
      between compiled basic blocks). Each slope is divided by the gas of one iteration and the
      largest result is used.
    - The pallet's `integrity_test` asserts that the derived ref time per gas is not zero.

    `WeightInfo` changes, which break every runtime that implements it with its own weights:

    - Removed: `basic_block_compilation(b)`, `instr(r)`, `instr_empty_loop(r)`.
    - Added: `interpreter_compile_per_instruction(n)`, `interpreter_compile_per_block(b)`,
      `interpreter_code_map_per_byte(c)`, `instr_load_chain_0(r)` to `instr_load_chain_7(r)`,
      `instr_indirect_jump(r)`.

    To migrate, regenerate the runtime's `pallet_revive` weights with the new benchmarks before
    upgrading. Renaming the functions is not enough: the ref time per gas and the compilation
    cost come from their slopes. Run the runtime's integrity tests on the new weights; they fail
    when a slope does not meet the conditions above.

    ```rust
    // Before
    fn basic_block_compilation(b: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    fn instr(r: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    fn instr_empty_loop(r: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }

    // After
    fn interpreter_compile_per_instruction(n: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    fn interpreter_compile_per_block(b: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    fn interpreter_code_map_per_byte(c: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    fn instr_load_chain_0(r: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    // ... one function per variant ...
    fn instr_load_chain_7(r: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    fn instr_indirect_jump(r: u32, ) -> Weight { ... }
    ```

    Other API changes:

    - `ContractBlob::prepare_call` and `CallSetup::prepare_call` lose their `aux_data_size`
      argument, and `PreparedCall` loses `aux_data_base` and `setup_aux_data`. No contract can
      access the aux data, and no benchmark uses it.
    - With the `runtime-benchmarks` feature, `PreparedCall` gains `memory_map`, `write_memory`,
      `set_reg` and `reset_interpreter_cache`. `VmBinaryModule` in `call_builder` gains
      `with_entry_block`, `with_branch_blocks`, `with_code_bytes`, `with_load_chain`,
      `with_indirect_jump_cycle`, `BRANCH_BLOCKS`, `MAX_CODE_BYTES`, `LOAD_CHAIN_SLOTS` and
      `LOAD_CHAIN_SLOT_BYTES`, and loses `instr`.
    - `pallet-revive-fixtures` gains the `SubCaller`, `SubCallerLarge`, `Sink`, `Reverter` and
      `Forwarder` Solidity contracts.

    Other runtime crates that use PolkaVM:

    - `sp-io`, `pallet-revive-uapi`, `sp-virtualization-test-fixture` and
      `substrate-wasm-builder` only change their PolkaVM dependency. No PolkaVM item appears in
      their API, and no migration is needed.
    - `sp-runtime-interface` re-exports the `polkavm_export` and `polkavm_import` macros of
      `polkavm-derive`. `polkavm-derive` 0.38 has the same source as 0.36, so the macros behave
      the same and no migration is needed.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The client crates that use PolkaVM move from `polkavm` 0.36 to 0.38.

    - `sc-executor-common` (`RuntimeBlob::as_polkavm_blob`) and `sc-executor-polkavm`
      (`create_runtime`) expose `polkavm::ProgramBlob` in their API, which is the 0.38 type.
      The `From` impls of `sc-executor-common` convert from the 0.38 types:
      `polkavm::program::ProgramParseError`, `polkavm::Error` and `polkavm::CompileError` into
      `WasmError`, and `polkavm::Error` into `Error`. Code that passes PolkaVM types to these
      crates must use `polkavm` 0.38.
    - `sc-virtualization` only changes its PolkaVM dependency. No PolkaVM item appears in its
      API, and no migration is needed.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The ref time charged per PolkaVM gas changes with the new weights. It covers the more
    expensive of dependent loads from the L2 cache and indirect jumps between compiled
    basic blocks. On Asset Hub Westend one gas costs 36618 ps of ref time, against 30303 ps
    before.

    Compiling contract code is charged as gas: on Asset Hub Westend 3 gas per basic block,
    1.579 gas per instruction and 0.015 gas per byte of the contract's code section. The caller
    of a PVM contract pays for loading its code, 2081 ps of ref time per byte of the code blob on
    Asset Hub Westend, which includes the callee's first per byte charge. A PVM contract pays the
    per byte charge again after a sub-call during which a PVM frame started: a call, delegate
    call or instantiation of a PVM contract, directly or through a pre-compile or an EVM
    contract.

    PVM execution and calls cost more weight than before. Contracts that pass fixed weight
    limits to their sub-calls may need to raise those limits.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: sc-executor-common
  bump: major
- name: sc-executor-polkavm
  bump: major
- name: sc-virtualization
  bump: minor
- name: sp-io
  bump: patch
- name: sp-runtime-interface
  bump: patch
- name: substrate-wasm-builder
  bump: minor
- name: sp-virtualization-test-fixture
  bump: patch
